From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:39:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): open phone Settings on its page list, not on
 General

Where the Settings menu covers the page (phones, and tablets held
upright), tapping the cog opened General and laid the menu drawer over
it: bare /settings redirected to General, and the drawer stayed open
over it with only a 56px strip of the page showing. Pages reached with
the drawer open, such as from a link in it, also opened under the menu.
Users read that as Settings jumping into General with the menu in the
way.

There, bare /settings now stays the page list: the route renders no
page, and the menu shows full width with no strip to tap and no swipe to
close. Choosing a page opens it with the menu closed, and so does any
other way onto a page (a deep link, a link elsewhere in the app, a
reload, or a tablet turned upright while the menu sat beside the page).
On a page the header's menu toggle becomes a Back chevron to the list,
which goes back through history when the page was opened from the list
and otherwise replaces the page with the list. The list marks no row as
current.

The desktop layout and the docked mobile layout (600px or wider at a
squarish or wider aspect) keep upstream's behaviour: bare /settings
opens General beside the menu, which leaves the page in view.

Not proposed upstream yet: upstream's shell deliberately keeps the phone
Settings menu open at bare /settings, so changing what it opens on is a
design question to raise there first.

Docs: none (phone Settings navigation; nothing to configure)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
